    "result_text": "The full build is green. Let me verify my fiscal-year logic against the observed run: the audit log showed `registrationDate=2026-09-07` \u2192 `membershipNumber=...-M26`. September is \u2265 July, so it falls in the fiscal year starting in 2026 \u2192 `FY26` / `M26`. Correct.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by its starting calendar year, labelled `FY<YY>`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/FiscalYear.java`** (new) \u2014 a static helper (matching the style of `AgeBand`/`MembershipLevel`/`OwnerLocality`) that computes the fiscal year of a date: `startYear()` returns the calendar year the fiscal year begins in (date's year if month \u2265 July, otherwise year\u22121), `twoDigit()` gives the two-digit form, and `labelForOwner()` returns `FY<YY>` from the owner's registration date.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014\n   - Added a `fiscalYear` mapping \u2192 `FiscalYear.labelForOwner(owner)`.\n   - Changed `membershipNumber`'s year segment from the raw registration-date year (`getYear() % 100`) to the **fiscal** two-digit year via `FiscalYear.twoDigit(...)`.\n\n   The registration date used is already the business-day-adjusted value (the controller rolls it forward and persists that), so both derive from the adjusted date.\n\n3. **`mapper/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 tenure bonus now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`FiscalYear.startYear(now) \u2212 FiscalYear.startYear(registration) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window; renamed the constant and updated the Javadoc.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` passes and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
